<InfoPage title="About Us" heading="About AtlasFigures" slug="about" type="AboutPage" updated="2026-11-25"
  description="AtlasFigures explains the world's population, time, economy and rankings country by country, with every figure sourced to the UN, World Bank and national statistics offices.">
  <p>AtlasFigures explains the world in numbers, one country at a time. Each country gets its own page, written around what makes its figures different, rather than the same template with the numbers swapped.</p>
  <h2>What we cover</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href={path('/population/')}>Population</a>: how many people live in each country, how crowded it is, and where it is heading by 2050.</li>
    <li>Time: local time, time differences and holidays (coming soon).</li>
    <li>Economy: income, growth and prices over time (coming soon).</li>
    <li>Rankings: countries compared on hundreds of measures (coming soon).</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <p>Every figure comes from an official or widely used source, such as the United Nations, the World Bank or a national statistics office, and every page lists its sources. Live counters are estimates built from official yearly figures; our <a href={path('/methodology/')}>methodology</a> explains exactly how.</p>
  <h2>Who writes AtlasFigures</h2>
  <p>Pages are researched and written by the AtlasFigures Editorial team. If you spot an error, please <a href={path('/corrections/')}>report it</a>: our corrections page explains what happens next and lists every correction we have made.</p>
</InfoPage>
